{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0148Zv3CdsmCuEFXJV6LQJm9","type":"tool_result","content":"150\t# Upper bound widened <0.157.0 -> <0.161.0; LOWER BOUND UNCHANGED at\n151\t# >=0.128.0 (widen-upper-only). The payload manifest is re-pinned in this\n152\t# same pack: payload sha256 112fae7a... for 0.160.0/aarch64-apple-darwin,\n153\t# npm_integrity from the PLATFORM artifact\n154\t# @openai/codex@0.160.0-darwin-arm64 (ADR-182 §5 step 2).\n155\t# Why now: Owner decision of 2026-10-02 (S362), recorded in PLAN-194 as plan\n156\t# B (manual re-pin from the newest mold, ADR-182 §5): this re-pin is the\n157\t# FIRST task of the v1.4.3 maintenance train. PLAN-194 pending decision 3\n158\t# (how the automatic pin is packaged) was NOT taken, so the automatic Codex\n159\t# pin (PLAN-194 W3) moves after v1.4.3 and its Security VETO stays raised;\n160\t# until it lands, every Codex upgrade goes through a pack generated like\n161\t# this one.\n162\t# Release window: executed OUTSIDE any open release window. GA v1.4.2 was\n163\t# cut on 2026-09-30 and no v1.4.3 tag exists; the ceremony refuses to run\n164\t# unless the v1.4.2 tag is an ancestor of HEAD. Doctrine (S355) met: this\n165\t# re-pin lands BEFORE the next release cut. Only the UPPER bound widens; the\n166\t# lower bound stays where it was (widen-upper-only, the only safe shape).\n167\t# The payload manifest remains the real supply-chain gate; this range is a\n168\t# version gate.\n169\t# Corpus rule: ADR-111 §2, restated as ADR-182 §5 step 5, reopens the corpus\n170\t# only on a MEASURED catch_rate shift >5pp on the locked corpus. That\n171\t# trigger is NOT EVALUABLE in this tree: no locked-corpus run exists for\n172\t# this bump (the runner's default corpus path is absent from this repository\n173\t# and its per-fixture review is still a stub), so it is unevaluated, not\n174\t# passed.\n175\t# The ADR-161 per-bump checklist is DEFERRED, as in S352, S356 and S357: it\n176\t# re-certifies Codex as a HOOK HOST, while what forces this re-pin is Codex\n177\t# as the rail REVIEWER. DECLARED CONSEQUENCE of that deferral, stated by\n178\t# shape: every consumer that reads this range as a version gate admits\n179\t# 0.160.x from this commit on, the installer's Codex-harness version-skew\n180\t# check (scripts/_codex_harness.sh) among them, while the hook evidence it\n181\t# names stays certified on 0.139.0.\n182\t# DECLARED CONSEQUENCE (same as S352, S356 and S357): this changes the\n183\t# INSTRUMENT. The rail reviewer becomes the 0.160.0 binary; rail\n184\t# measurements taken before and after this commit are NOT comparable, and\n185\t# the first rail round on 0.160.0 is a re-test. What the reviewer serves is\n186\t# chosen by the Owner's Codex config, not by this pin: measured on\n187\t# 2026-10-02 (S362 probe of 0.160.0 in a disposable npm prefix) as model\n188\t# gpt-6-astra at reasoning effort xhigh. A change of that config changes the\n189\t# instrument without touching these bytes.\n190\t# Residual, by shape: the pin attests ONE executable, the\n191\t# aarch64-apple-darwin payload at the manifest path. Every other executable\n192\t# is outside the sha: the sibling executables the platform tarball carries\n193\t# beside it, the payloads of the other npm platforms, and the launcher of\n194\t# the main package (bin/codex.js). Same posture as every earlier generation,\n195\t# not a regression of this pack.\n196\t# Current compatibility floor (Onda6B): stable Codex CLI releases at or above\n197\t# 0.128.0 are compatible version evidence. This unbounded range is not a\n198\t# payload-hash attestation; codex-cli-pin-manifest.json remains that gate.\n199\t>=0.128.0\n200\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"58d86da0-a33a-4fc7-a08e-6d4c6f14f756","uuid":"8694b1fb-7736-4853-9cb5-ec9c1bc63be5","timestamp":"2026-11-13T16:22:21.541Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repa