{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016TrRjYYGJ6Et7sjpQgV5SX","type":"tool_result","content":"40\t\n41\tThe cost is explicit export lists, binding logic, and a requirement to test\n42\tboth the real output and patch points. A plain import/re-export would leave\n43\tfunctions looking up globals in their implementation module, breaking patches\n44\ton the historical facade. Reload and mutable state require particular care.\n45\t\n46\t## AST and integrity boundaries\n47\t\n48\tSource-level consumers must be checked individually. In particular,\n49\t`check-audit-registry-coverage.py` parses `audit_emit.py` for literal\n50\t`_KNOWN_ACTIONS` and `emit_` definitions; moving a function changes what that\n51\tAST can see. Named `audit-query.py` delegates and the functional `audit_emit.py`\n52\t`iter_events` delegate preserve the declarations expected by the read-API\n53\tguard, not the entire pre-decomposition AST. Runtime exports and\n54\tAST-visible declarations are different contracts; neither proves the other.\n55\t\n56\tImport failure policy is owned by each entry point, not by this architectural\n57\trecord. The separate import-integrity work for `check_canonical_edit.py`\n58\taddresses its component failure path; this ADR does not claim equivalent\n59\tfail-closed behavior for every package, nor that imports attest code integrity.\n60\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"58d86da0-a33a-4fc7-a08e-6d4c6f14f756","uuid":"113b89d9-330c-4117-9176-ac61489b1fab","timestamp":"2026-11-13T16:27:35.154Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.nUJTgA/tree/.claude/adr/ADR-202-kernel-and-hooks-modularization.md","content":"\nThe cost is explicit export lists, binding logic, and a requirement to test\nboth the real output and patch points. A plain import/re-export would leave\nfunctions looking up globals in their implementation module, breaking patches\non the historical facade. Reload and mutable state require particular care.\n\n## AST and integrity boundaries\n\nSource-level consumers must be checked individually. In particular,\n`check-audit-registry-coverage.py` parses `audit_emit.py` for literal\n`_KNOWN_ACTIONS` and `emit_` definitions; moving a function changes what that\nAST can see. Named `audit-query.py` delegates and the functional `audit_emit.py`\n`iter_events` delegate preserve the declarations expected by the read-API\nguard, not the entire pre-decomposition AST. Runtime exports and\nAST-visible declarations are different contracts; neither proves the other.\n\nImport failure policy is owned by each entry point, not by this architectural\nrecord. The separate import-integrity work for `check_canonical_edit.py`\naddresses its component failure path; this ADR does not claim equivalent\nfail-closed behavior for every package, nor that imports attest code integrity.\n","numLines":21,"startLine":40,"totalLines":60}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_016TrRjYYGJ6Et7sjpQgV5SX","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
