uture Codex whose hook discovery has changed. The arming check prints no skew warning, although the fixtures were recorded on 0.139.0 and CODEX_VERIFIED_VERSION is 0.160.0. Untrusted or changed hooks are silent no-ops on Codex, so this warning was the operator's only version signal.\\n- CHANGELOG [1.4.4] lines 207-208 mention only the \\\"verified against 0.160.0\\\" banner. A reader learns the warning is gone only by combining [1.4.3] lines 731-733 with [1.4.4] line 200.\\n- Minimal fix: say it plainly in Known-open, or make _codex_harness.sh warn above CODEX_VERIFIED_VERSION whatever the pin's upper bound.\\n\\nP2-3. Stale text about the Codex pin.\\n- codex-cli-pin.txt:165-166 still calls \\\"widen-upper-only\\\" \\\"the only safe shape\\\", directly above the new unbounded line.\\n- INSTALL.md:1028-1030 still says that in the framework checkout a payload mismatch blocks (fail-closed). On the compatible/version_floor_only route that is no longer true, as CHANGELOG lines 184-193 already say.\\n- Minimal fix: amend that comment and that paragraph.\\n\\nP2-4. Stale docstrings.\\n- defense.py emit_learning_rail_disabled says \\\"four learning-loop rails\\\", but _LEARNING_RAIL_ENUM (lifecycle_schemas.py:508) has five, bash_indirect included.\\n- emit_ceo_boot_check_skipped cites \\\"15 Tier-S + 10 Tier-A\\\", but the registry has 25 Tier-S.\\n- Cosmetic only.\\n\\nP2-5. A crash-orphaned temp file of the shard cursor is never collected (pre-existing since v1.4.0).\\n- Where: context_pressure.py:96-118 and 168-172.\\n- The temp file \\\"..gc-shard-cursor.<pid>.<rand>.tmp\\\" never matches the marker prefix after the one-dot strip, so the GC skips it. It is left behind only if the process is killed between the O_EXCL open and os.replace.\\n- Minimal fix: let the sweep also collect aged \\\".<_GC_SHARD_COUNTER_NAME>.*.tmp\\\" files.\\n\\nNOT VERIFIED HERE\\n- The sha256 values in gate-scripts-manifest.txt (no hashing tool, redacted tree).\\n- The facade-side deletion from audit_emit.py and the remaining parts (writer, generic_dispatch_*, and the others) are in later payloads. Conditions 1-4, 6, 8 and 11-14 are not exercised by this payload, and nothing in it contradicts them.\",\"decision\":\"GO-WITH-CONDITIONS\",\"sentence\":\"In payload 1 the declared conditions that apply (5, 7, 9 and 10) hold against the code, the audit_emit split binds every exported name to the facade with infrastructure failures still failing open, and the only findings are P2 follow-ups. The release can therefore proceed only under its declared conditions, chiefly the declared unbounded Codex pin.\"}","structured_output":{"report":"SCOPE OF PAYLOAD 1/32\nVersion files (.claude-plugin/plugin.json, .claude-plugin/marketplace.json, .claude/.framework-version), .claude/commands/ceo-boot.md, .claude/governance/codex-cli-pin.txt, .claude/governance/gate-scripts-manifest.txt, and the first 15 files of the new .claude/hooks/_lib/_audit_emit_parts/ package (__init__, actions, actions_core, actions_extended, adapters, boot_schemas, compaction, confidence, context_pressure, defense, federation_persona, federation_schemas, finalization).\n\nWHAT WAS CHECKED, AND THE RESULT\n1. Version bump: the three version files now say 1.4.4 and agree with each other.\n2. ceo-boot.md \"24 -> 25 Tier-S\": true. TIER_S_CHECKS asserts exactly 25 (.claude/hooks/_lib/_ceo_boot_parts/scheduled_cache.py:370).\n3. codex-cli-pin.txt goes from \">=0.128.0,<0.161.0\" to \">=0.128.0\" (no upper bound). Every consumer handles a missing upper bound:\n   - the release validator: .github/scripts/validate-pair-rail-verdict.py:345-358 and 609-624;\n   - the installer's harness script: scripts/_codex_harness.sh:77-86;\n   - the kit generator still refuses a version below cli_currency.CODEX_VERSION_FLOOR even with the manifest's sha: .claude/plans/PLAN-198/kit/gen_envelope.py:1074-1100.\n   This matches conditions 9 and 10 and CHANGELOG [1.4.4] lines 184-208 and 393-397. Conditions 9 and 10 hold.\n4. gate-scripts-manifest.txt: three hashes change. I could not recompute them (no shell here, and the tree copy is redacted). Only the framework's own CI reads this file (release.yml, smoke-install.yml, npm-publish.yml, ownership-nightly.yml). A wrong hash would block the framework's own release; adopters do not receive .claude/governance/.\n5. Moved code: how _audit_emit_parts/__init__.py install() works.\n   - It rebinds each part function onto the facade's globals. Monkeypatches on audit_emit, \"global\" statements and late-bound helpers therefore resolve in the facade.\n   - None of the parts has a decorator or a class, so no function keeps a part module's globals.\n   - No part exports a lock or any other object that deepcopy cannot copy. re.Pattern objects copy fine.\n   - The names exported by this payload's parts are not duplicated across parts, and no part overrides a name the facade defines before install() (_KNOWN_ACTIONS, EVENT_SCHEMA_V2, emit_credential_rotation_due). The only exception is the dead actions.py, which is never installed (P2-1).\n   - Every name the payload's parts use resolves in the facade namespace. zlib, os, time, Path and the typing names are imported at audit_emit.py:4-12. The helpers come from writer.py (_write_event, _breadcrumb, _normalize_rotation_trigger), tokens_boot.py (_scrub_ceo_boot_event, _is_sha256_hex, the _SUBAGENT_LIFECYCLE_* names), harness_schemas.py and lifecycle_schemas.py.\n   - Each part's __all__ lists every top-level definition in it.\n   - Production consumers I spot-checked still resolve: _compaction_plan_id_ok, the _CONTEXT_PRESSURE_* names, should_emit_context_pressure, clear_context_pressure_marker, _CONFIG_CHANGE_LAYERS, _ATLAS_REGISTRY, and the emit_* wrappers called by SessionStart, check_confidence_gate, the bash_safety parts, the mcp-server and ceo-escalation-detector.\n   - No part uses __file__.\n   - Python 3.9 and standard library only: every part uses \"from __future__ import annotations\", FunctionType is called with its five positional arguments, and nothing uses 3.10+ syntax.\n6. Fidelity of the moved code: the functions in context_pressure.py match their v1.4.0-GA text in .claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-ga/diff-ga-6.patch:880-1131.\n   - Writes: the temp file is opened with O_EXCL|O_NOFOLLOW and mode 0600, then renamed over the target with os.replace. unlink removes a symlink itself, not what it points to. All I/O errors fail open.\n7. Fail direction:\n   - Every governance-hook import of audit_emit I checked is wrapped in try/except, so an import failure of any of the 33 parts fails open: _lib/canonical_edit/*, check_arbitration_kernel.py:585 and 647, _bash_safety_parts/normalization.py:229, and check_agent_spawn.py:74-79 (which imports the audit_emit_dispatch shim).\n   - _safe_verifier_outcome returns \"\" when the redactor cannot be imported. That is the data-minimizing direction and is correct.\n   - No inversion found.\n8. Condition 5: the row .claude/hooks/_lib/_audit_emit_parts/**/* is at check_arbitration_kernel.py:312. \"**\" matches zero or more segments (check_arbitration_kernel.py:376-389), so files directly under the package are kernel too. Condition 7 holds for audit_emit: the facade is 496 lines and the logic lives in the parts.\n\nP0: none.\n\nNEW FINDINGS (annex): none at P1.\n\nP2 FOLLOW-UPS\nP2-1. A duplicate action registry that runtime never reads.\n- Where: .claude/hooks/_lib/_audit_emit_parts/actions.py:1-16, actions_core.py:1-4 and actions_extended.py:1-4, against .claude/hooks/_lib/audit_emit.py:45-377 (the literal _KNOWN_ACTIONS) and 413-452 (the install() list, which has no \"actions\").\n- Failure scenario: a maintainer registers a new action in actions_extended.py, following its own in-file comments (\"Registered via kernel-override ...\"), and gets through the kernel override. The runtime registry is still the facade literal, so the action stays unknown and its emits are dropped to a breadcrumb. check-audit-registry-coverage.py and the reality ledger also read the literal, so no gate notices.\n- Misleading docstrings: actions_core.py and actions_extended.py say they are \"combined by schemas_actions\", and that module does not exist. actions.py says the facade exports it, which it does not.\n- No test checks that the two registries agree. Today they match: 234 + 97 = 331 entries.\n- Minimal fix: delete the three files, or add a test asserting _audit_emit_parts.actions._KNOWN_ACTIONS == audit_emit._KNOWN_ACTIONS and reword the docstrings to call them a mirror.\n\nP2-2. With no upper bound on the pin, the --harness codex VERSION SKEW warning no longer fires for any newer Codex.\n- Where: .claude/governance/codex-cli-pin.txt:199, with scripts/_codex_harness.sh:77-86 and 459-461.\n- Failure scenario: an adopter installs with --harness codex on a future Codex whose hook discovery has changed. The arming check prints no skew warning, although the fixtures were recorded on 0.139.0 and CODEX_VERIFIED_VERSION is 0.160.0. Untrusted or changed hooks are silent no-ops on Codex, so this warning was the operator's only version signal.\n- CHANGELOG [1.4.4] lines 207-208 mention only the \"verified against 0.160.0\" banner. A reader learns the warning is gone only by combining [1.4.3] lines 731-733 with [1.4.4] line 200.\n- Minimal fix: say it plainly in Known-open, or make _codex_harness.sh warn above CODEX_VERIFIED_VERSION whatever the pin's upper bound.\n\nP2-3. Stale text about the Codex pin.\n- codex-cli-pin.txt:165-166 still calls \"widen-upper-only\" \"the only safe shape\", directly above the new unbounded line.\n- INSTALL.md:1028-1030 still says that in the framework checkout a payload mismatch blocks (fail-closed). On the compatible/version_floor_only route that is no longer true, as CHANGELOG lines 184-193 already say.\n- Minimal fix: amend that comment and that paragraph.\n\nP2-4. Stale docstrings.\n- defense.py emit_learning_rail_disabled says \"four learning-loop rails\", but _LEARNING_RAIL_ENUM (lifecycle_schemas.py:508) has five, bash_indirect included.\n- emit_ceo_boot_check_skipped cites \"15 Tier-S + 10 Tier-A\", but the registry has 25 Tier-S.\n- Cosmetic only.\n\nP2-5. A crash-orphaned temp file of the shard cursor is never collected (pre-existing since v1.4.0).\n- Where: context_pressure.py:96-118 and 168-172.\n- The temp file \"..gc-shard-cursor.<pid>.<rand>.tmp\" never matches the marker prefix after the one-dot strip, so the GC skips it. It is left behind only if the process is killed between the O_EXCL open and os.replace.\n- Minimal fix: let the sweep also collect aged \".<_GC_SHARD_COUNTER_NAME>.*.tmp\" files.\n\nNOT VERIFIED HERE\n- The sha256 values in gate-scripts-manifest.txt (no hashing tool, redacted tree).\n- The facade-side deletion from audit_emit.py and the remaining parts (writer, generic_dispatch_*, and the others) are in later payloads. Conditions 1-4, 6, 8 and 11-14 are not exercised by this payload, and nothing in it contradicts them.","decision":"GO-WITH-CONDITIONS","sentence":"In payload 1 the declared conditions that apply (5, 7, 9 and 10) hold against the code, the audit_emit split binds every exported name to the facade with infrastructure failures still failing open, and the only findings are P2 follow-ups. The release can therefore proceed only under its declared conditions, chiefly the declared unbounded Codex pin."},"ttft_ms":19914,"type":"result","duration_ms":500790,"uuid":"67e02a27-ec3d-4af6-bef9-5f9ed72a6f7a","ttft_stream_ms":4088,"time_to_request_ms":41,"first_content_frame_ms":4088,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"model_usage_since_last_result":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":108,"outputTokens":42975,"cacheReadInputTokens":9598024,"cacheCreationInputTokens":235908,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":4.666800800000001,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":29034,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":235908,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5